                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Should have played earlier, very good CPU puzzle game. Quite different than Turing Complete and I like it takes a different approach: you don't build boolean tables or elementary structures, but instead it focuses next on latency and teaches you how/why pipelining works. Components are pre-made for you. Neat.\n\nI.e. I thought I knew in abstract what pipeline does in the CPU, yes. But it hits that sweet spot of \"ah, that's why! wow\" when for the first time you need to implement branching in a pipeline.\n\nYes yes, game could use some polish, I was frustrated in places. I just asked chatgpt to give me a hint or direction and I was fine. Solving levels are exciting.\n\n9/10, very cool, esp. later levels.",
